Description: Widgets: paint a window once per eye while its style shows depth
 .
 A style that draws its elements in depth (Union on Stereo KWin) sets the
 window's _q_stereo_depth while the compositor shows depth inside the window.
 The repaint manager then paints the window once per eye into a backing store
 twice as wide, the left eye first, setting the window's _q_stereo_eye for
 the parts the style moves itself, and sets _q_stereo_pair for the platform.
 .
 Each widget moves by its own eye shift from its _q_stereo_parallax (device
 pixels, positive when nearer than the screen), split as Stereo KWin splits a
 parallax: the left eye p - p / 2 to the right for nearer, the right eye
 -(p / 2). A widget without a parallax moves with the widget it is in. A
 widget nearer than what it lies on is drawn whole, over its surroundings; a
 deeper one is seen through its own rectangle, cut to it. Every eye is
 painted whole, opaque widgets do not hide what is beneath them, and the
 backing store is not scrolled, since a widget's place is not the same in the
 two eyes. A window with render-to-texture widgets is painted once, and so
 is one with a frame the client draws around it (frameMargins(), on Wayland a
 client-side decoration), which would be drawn into one half only.
 .
 Without _q_stereo_depth nothing changes: the window is painted once, as
 before, which tst_qwidgetrepaintmanager's paintOncePerEye checks too.
